WEBVTT

00:05.967 --> 00:08.807
[♪ opening theme song playing]

01:45.277 --> 01:47.617
[bleating]

01:53.537 --> 01:55.957
[GIRL] My lady, where are you?

01:57.537 --> 01:59.207
My lady!

02:00.917 --> 02:02.087
[sighs]

02:02.167 --> 02:04.717
Goodness,
what are you doing out here?

02:04.797 --> 02:07.087
It's time for you
to get ready to leave.

02:08.967 --> 02:09.967
[TÖREGENE]
Be right there.

02:15.057 --> 02:16.477
[wind blows]

02:18.267 --> 02:20.687
[TÖREGENE]
Farewell, Naiman.

02:21.977 --> 02:23.197
♪

02:23.857 --> 02:26.237
[TÖREGENE] As someone born
into the Naimans

02:26.317 --> 02:28.947
whose nation lay far
to the west of here,

02:29.367 --> 02:32.617
it was arranged that I would
marry into the Merkits,

02:32.697 --> 02:34.747
with whom we shared an alliance.

02:35.327 --> 02:36.747
[GIRL] I wonder about
the Merkit tribes

02:36.827 --> 02:38.037
and what their lives are like.

02:38.327 --> 02:39.167
[TÖREGENE'S SISTER-IN-LAW]
They live in the woods

02:39.247 --> 02:40.247
just to the north.

02:40.587 --> 02:42.627
Many of them are skilled bowmen
called Mergen.

02:42.707 --> 02:44.217
Mergen?

02:44.297 --> 02:46.177
They're known
as the Mergen people,

02:46.257 --> 02:47.837
hence the name "Merkits."

02:47.927 --> 02:51.007
[TÖREGENE] In other words,
barbaric hunters.

02:51.097 --> 02:52.257
[Töregene's sister-in-law
sniffles]

02:52.347 --> 02:54.307
[TÖREGENE]
Well, it matters not.

02:54.387 --> 02:56.097
I am nothing
but a valuable gift.

02:57.097 --> 02:59.397
No different
from a precious gemstone

02:59.477 --> 03:00.977
or a fine fur pelt.

03:02.107 --> 03:03.777
But that's all well.

03:03.857 --> 03:07.697
I'm fulfilling my role,
and accept it with pride.

03:17.787 --> 03:18.877
[senior wife chuckles]

03:19.457 --> 03:21.627
[TÖREGENE] So this is where
the Merkits live.

03:21.707 --> 03:24.257
It's much drearier
than I expected.

03:24.337 --> 03:25.507
[indistinct chatter]

03:25.587 --> 03:27.467
[TÖREGENE]
Why are there so few men?

03:27.547 --> 03:28.927
-[DAYIR] Töregene.
-Uh?

03:29.717 --> 03:30.597
Glad you're safe.

03:31.717 --> 03:33.967
I am sorry, I know this isn't
much of a welcome.

03:34.057 --> 03:37.267
Are you startled to learn
your husband's such an old man?

03:37.347 --> 03:38.517
No.

03:40.937 --> 03:42.317
Well, so be it.

03:42.857 --> 03:46.147
Marrying a much older man
is far from rare.

03:47.987 --> 03:51.117
And yet,
after our wedding ceremony,

03:51.197 --> 03:53.577
Dayir never made any advances.

03:56.407 --> 03:58.457
On the contrary...

03:58.537 --> 04:00.377
So, you'll be going away again?

04:00.457 --> 04:03.377
Please forgive me
for always leaving you behind.

04:04.127 --> 04:05.837
And why do we keep moving camps?

04:06.507 --> 04:08.797
It seems like
we just arrived here.

04:08.877 --> 04:09.837
[Dayir sighs]

04:10.257 --> 04:12.887
We can't stay
in one place for too long.

04:13.217 --> 04:15.387
-You had best get going now.
-[gasps]

04:15.847 --> 04:17.017
[DAYIR] Chuu!

04:20.687 --> 04:24.147
-If you need anything, I'm here.
-Thank you.

04:24.227 --> 04:25.817
-I, uh--
-[GIRL] Mistress...

04:25.897 --> 04:27.817
What should I do with this?

04:28.147 --> 04:29.777
Oh, well, let's see now.

04:31.157 --> 04:32.657
[TÖREGENE]
Do all of the other tribes

04:32.737 --> 04:35.197
keep moving their camps
as often as we do?

04:35.277 --> 04:36.997
-Right over there. Please.
-[TÖREGENE] No.

04:37.077 --> 04:39.617
There's something strange
going on here.

04:39.707 --> 04:42.667
It feels as if we're fleeing
from something.

04:45.337 --> 04:48.877
Well, I suppose
there's no use in worrying.

04:49.547 --> 04:52.387
I'm only here to be a gemstone.

04:52.467 --> 04:55.887
And what good would it do
for a gemstone to be concerned?

04:58.017 --> 04:58.927
[breathes uneasily]

05:00.187 --> 05:02.557
I want to go back to Naiman.

05:04.517 --> 05:06.227
[birds chirping]

05:08.107 --> 05:10.447
-[bird screeching]
-[Töregene pants]

05:12.067 --> 05:13.947
They won't notice
if I go missing.

05:14.777 --> 05:16.907
I know Chieftain Dayir won't.

05:16.987 --> 05:19.537
Nor will anybody else
who's in the tribe.

05:20.577 --> 05:21.657
-[GIRL] Hold on!
-[Töregene gasps]

05:23.417 --> 05:24.917
Stay right where you are!

05:25.667 --> 05:26.667
[gasps]

05:31.167 --> 05:32.337
[panting]

05:32.427 --> 05:33.797
That was close, wasn't it?

05:34.297 --> 05:35.637
Are you all right?

05:38.677 --> 05:41.137
You truly live up
to your title of Mergen.

05:41.227 --> 05:43.477
Ah, not really. Easy shot.

05:43.557 --> 05:44.807
Huh? Oh my...

05:44.897 --> 05:47.147
You must be Töregene,
aren't you?

05:47.227 --> 05:49.477
Then that means
you're my new mother.

05:50.857 --> 05:51.947
[TÖREGENE] Huh?

05:52.487 --> 05:54.027
My name is Khulan.

05:54.107 --> 05:55.197
I'm Dayir's daughter.

05:55.277 --> 05:56.527
Qultuqan...

05:56.987 --> 05:58.237
Is my name.

05:59.197 --> 06:00.997
-[chuckles softly]
-[Khulan laughs]

06:01.077 --> 06:03.077
[TÖREGENE]
Khulan was Dayir's child.

06:03.157 --> 06:05.827
And Qultuqan was the child
of another chieftain.

06:05.917 --> 06:08.457
[KHULAN] See that? If you start
going down this river,

06:08.547 --> 06:11.007
it splits off into the Qara
and Dal rivers.

06:11.087 --> 06:13.127
Further down,
both of them wind around

06:13.217 --> 06:15.427
until they feed
into the Selenge River.

06:15.507 --> 06:18.177
And that's the place where
Qultuqan and I were born.

06:18.257 --> 06:19.427
You were?

06:19.927 --> 06:21.847
If you go all the way
down the rivers,

06:21.927 --> 06:24.347
do you know where every single
one of them ends up?

06:24.437 --> 06:25.767
[TÖREGENE] Hmm...

06:25.847 --> 06:26.807
[Khulan grunts]

06:26.897 --> 06:28.647
So you know
the star to the north

06:28.727 --> 06:30.107
that doesn't move at all?

06:30.187 --> 06:31.147
♪

06:31.227 --> 06:32.397
[KHULAN] Right underneath it,

06:32.487 --> 06:34.527
there's the biggest hole
you can imagine.

06:34.607 --> 06:35.817
And that's the place

06:36.197 --> 06:38.777
where the rivers from
all over the entire world flow.

06:38.867 --> 06:41.827
Wow. I've never heard
that before.

06:41.907 --> 06:43.367
[Khulan chuckles]

06:43.447 --> 06:45.787
Well, it's not like
you've seen it for yourself.

06:46.417 --> 06:48.207
Come on. Cut it out.

06:48.287 --> 06:49.497
Is that true?

06:49.587 --> 06:51.667
Neither of us
has the power like a kam

06:51.757 --> 06:52.957
to communicate with spirits.

06:53.047 --> 06:54.667
My father is a kam, though.

06:55.177 --> 06:56.177
And he has been out

06:56.257 --> 06:58.177
where the rivers
end a lot of times!

06:58.717 --> 07:01.887
His soul turns into a bird,
and he flies way up there.

07:02.347 --> 07:03.467
A kam?

07:03.557 --> 07:06.307
Hmm. I wish
I could do things like that

07:06.387 --> 07:08.147
and have kam powers, too.

07:08.227 --> 07:10.687
Or be somebody who has
great skills with a bow.

07:10.767 --> 07:12.477
You are a pretty terrible shot.

07:12.567 --> 07:14.487
Enough! Hold your tongue!

07:14.567 --> 07:16.277
You said it yourself, Khulan!

07:16.357 --> 07:18.237
-[KHULAN] I'm serious.
-[QULTUQAN] So am I.

07:18.317 --> 07:19.817
[Töregene laughs]

07:19.907 --> 07:22.117
It looks like
we got you laughing.

07:22.197 --> 07:23.997
[TÖREGENE]
Oh, pardon me. [laughs]

07:24.077 --> 07:26.247
[Khulan laughs]

07:26.327 --> 07:27.787
[Qultuqan laughs]

07:27.867 --> 07:29.037
♪

07:29.827 --> 07:31.127
[TÖREGENE] On that day,

07:31.207 --> 07:33.957
it seemed like something
deep inside had changed.

07:34.047 --> 07:35.127
♪

07:36.047 --> 07:38.547
It felt as though
the very world around me

07:38.637 --> 07:41.677
stirred my soul
in so many different ways.

07:52.147 --> 07:55.487
I experienced
true laughter and joy.

08:06.657 --> 08:09.827
Discontent and a sense
of sorrow too.

08:09.917 --> 08:10.997
♪

08:22.467 --> 08:24.467
As the days passed by,

08:24.557 --> 08:26.847
I came to love
every moment here.

08:37.397 --> 08:38.897
And then for the first time,

08:39.647 --> 08:40.947
I understood.

08:46.697 --> 08:48.907
Wake up, everyone!

08:49.867 --> 08:51.287
We must flee.

08:51.367 --> 08:52.497
What happened?

08:52.577 --> 08:54.087
Our chieftains' armies
have been bested!

08:54.167 --> 08:56.587
-[all gasp]
-The enemy will be here soon!

08:57.297 --> 08:58.757
-[horse neighs]
-[grunts]

08:58.837 --> 09:01.837
[soldiers yelling distantly]

09:01.927 --> 09:04.387
[screaming]

09:04.467 --> 09:05.847
Into the woods!

09:06.257 --> 09:07.807
[panting]

09:07.887 --> 09:10.727
[QULTUQAN]
Khulan, Töregene, come this way.

09:10.807 --> 09:11.807
[KHULAN] Qultuqan!

09:15.057 --> 09:16.687
[people crying]

09:16.767 --> 09:18.187
[QULTUQAN'S BROTHER]
How much did they plunder?

09:18.277 --> 09:20.487
[QULTUQAN]
Qudu's family is gone,

09:20.567 --> 09:22.357
as are Chilaun's wife
and children.

09:23.617 --> 09:24.867
[DAYIR] Töregene!

09:25.327 --> 09:26.697
[KHULAN] Father, you're here.

09:26.777 --> 09:28.947
[DAYIR]
You must have been scared.

09:29.037 --> 09:31.407
I want to thank you
for protecting our Khulan.

09:31.497 --> 09:32.497
Mm-mm.

09:32.577 --> 09:34.707
She was the one
who protected me.

09:34.787 --> 09:37.207
What on earth is going on here?

09:37.797 --> 09:40.047
So, the Naimans never told you
of the danger

09:40.127 --> 09:41.467
we have been facing?

09:42.217 --> 09:44.337
Well, I suppose
I cannot blame them.

09:45.887 --> 09:47.887
Our people have a true enemy.

09:47.967 --> 09:50.017
Temüjin of the Mongols.

09:51.927 --> 09:56.187
The vicious man who now bears
the title of Genghis Khan.

09:59.437 --> 10:01.027
Genghis Khan?

10:01.107 --> 10:02.987
[DAYIR]
As long as I can remember,

10:03.067 --> 10:06.487
we Merkits have engaged
in skirmishes with the Mongols.

10:06.567 --> 10:08.697
They have taken many
of our families

10:08.777 --> 10:10.947
and deprived us
of our possessions.

10:11.037 --> 10:13.207
Yet we always
struck back in kind.

10:14.617 --> 10:17.957
But with Temüjin
as their leader, it all changed.

10:18.037 --> 10:20.707
And the very balance
of the steppe was lost.

10:21.337 --> 10:22.837
The reason you were
given away

10:22.917 --> 10:24.797
to become the wife of an old man

10:24.877 --> 10:28.257
was to strengthen our alliance
against the Mongols.

10:28.847 --> 10:33.307
That said, it seems the end
may finally be near.

10:34.137 --> 10:37.107
Say, brother,
if the Mongols do win,

10:37.187 --> 10:38.557
what will become of us then?

10:38.647 --> 10:39.977
You have to ask?

10:40.067 --> 10:41.357
They'll slaughter the men

10:41.437 --> 10:43.487
and take all our women
and children.

10:44.817 --> 10:47.367
[QULTUQAN] I'm really afraid.
I don't want to die.

10:48.027 --> 10:50.907
[QULTUQAN'S BROTHER] Fool!
You call yourself a Merkit man?

10:50.987 --> 10:51.997
[Dayir sighs]

10:59.837 --> 11:00.877
[MAN] Usun.

11:00.957 --> 11:02.297
Usun.

11:02.957 --> 11:05.297
Usun. Means "flowing river."

11:05.797 --> 11:07.257
For his role as our kam,

11:07.337 --> 11:09.637
the earth bestowed
that title upon him.

11:10.097 --> 11:11.177
Listen well.

11:11.467 --> 11:13.927
No one is to utter
a word until I've finished.

11:15.557 --> 11:19.057
For I shall beseech
the spirits to guide me.

11:20.807 --> 11:22.357
[wind blows]

11:24.187 --> 11:25.437
[DAYIR] Oh, spirits,

11:25.527 --> 11:27.527
lift me up to the heavens.

11:27.907 --> 11:30.527
Show me what lies in our future.

11:30.947 --> 11:32.407
[inhales deeply]

11:32.487 --> 11:34.117
[♪ drum beating]

11:34.747 --> 11:35.867
[breathing heavily]

11:49.087 --> 11:50.387
[wind blowing]

12:16.327 --> 12:17.957
[exclaims]

12:20.917 --> 12:22.417
♪

12:27.257 --> 12:28.217
[gasps]

12:33.547 --> 12:36.387
[Dayir exclaims]

12:36.467 --> 12:37.517
♪

12:50.447 --> 12:51.697
[Dayir groans]

12:51.777 --> 12:52.867
Usun.

12:52.947 --> 12:54.237
[Dayir pants]

12:55.987 --> 12:58.077
Khulan, are you there?

12:58.157 --> 12:59.247
[Khulan gasps]

13:00.577 --> 13:02.127
Yes, I'm right here, Father.

13:02.917 --> 13:05.167
I could see a very lush steppe.

13:05.537 --> 13:08.877
A river branching
and feeding into many others.

13:09.587 --> 13:12.047
And when I followed the river
to its source,

13:12.137 --> 13:15.297
atop a mountain that was
as tall as the heavens,

13:15.387 --> 13:17.427
I found a pure riverhead.

13:18.137 --> 13:20.557
All those rivers
were bloodlines.

13:20.637 --> 13:23.017
And they signified
that Mongol progeny

13:23.097 --> 13:25.557
will soon be spreading across
this great land.

13:25.647 --> 13:26.767
So...

13:26.857 --> 13:29.317
We are destined to lose
to the Mongols.

13:29.397 --> 13:30.527
[all exclaim]

13:31.947 --> 13:33.277
Then does that mean

13:33.357 --> 13:35.577
each one of us
is going to be killed?

13:35.657 --> 13:38.037
No. I won't allow that
to happen.

13:38.117 --> 13:39.247
[Khulan gasps]

13:39.537 --> 13:40.747
[DAYIR]
According to the spirits,

13:40.827 --> 13:42.367
the Merkit blood will live on

13:42.457 --> 13:44.377
even after we've
surrendered to them.

13:44.457 --> 13:47.747
Do you really think Genghis Khan
will show us any mercy?

13:47.837 --> 13:50.297
Yes, but we'll have to give
appropriate tribute

13:50.377 --> 13:52.337
in exchange
for such a thing, of course.

13:52.417 --> 13:53.377
[all sigh]

13:54.007 --> 13:57.637
[DAYIR] A pure riverhead
to appease Genghis Khan.

13:57.717 --> 14:00.057
-I shall offer my daughter.
-[all gasp]

14:00.137 --> 14:01.347
Khulan.

14:02.017 --> 14:04.017
[grunts] You mustn't!

14:04.097 --> 14:06.107
I won't allow you
to sacrifice her.

14:06.557 --> 14:09.317
She's a human
with her own mind and will!

14:09.397 --> 14:11.987
Not a gemstone or a fur pelt!

14:12.067 --> 14:13.147
[whimpers]

14:14.647 --> 14:18.077
She's not... [cries softly]
like me.

14:20.617 --> 14:24.997
Töregene, thank you so much,
but I will be fine.

14:25.457 --> 14:26.707
Khulan?

14:28.247 --> 14:31.417
In all honesty,
I am happy, Father.

14:31.707 --> 14:33.507
I've always resented
being a girl

14:33.587 --> 14:35.507
and needing others' protection.

14:35.587 --> 14:36.797
But this way,

14:36.887 --> 14:38.097
I can serve as the arrow

14:38.177 --> 14:39.717
that will keep
each one of you safe.

14:39.807 --> 14:41.257
You mean...

14:41.677 --> 14:43.767
Merkits are masters of the bow.

14:44.267 --> 14:45.977
And as a daughter
of the Mergens,

14:46.057 --> 14:48.307
this is my chance
to take down a wolf.

14:48.977 --> 14:50.317
♪

14:53.147 --> 14:55.487
[TÖREGENE]
So we gathered together

14:55.567 --> 14:57.407
and surrendered to the Mongols.

14:58.567 --> 15:01.277
Khulan managed to sever
the chains of hostility

15:01.367 --> 15:04.497
that had bound the Mongols
and Merkits for so long,

15:05.657 --> 15:07.997
saving countless Merkit lives.

15:08.577 --> 15:09.537
♪

15:12.337 --> 15:14.667
But Qultuqan
and the other Merkit tribes

15:14.757 --> 15:16.377
didn't join the rest of us,

15:16.467 --> 15:18.467
choosing to stand
in bold defiance

15:18.547 --> 15:19.757
until the very end.

15:19.847 --> 15:21.927
Fleeing westward on foot.

15:22.927 --> 15:24.267
♪

15:25.557 --> 15:27.517
That should be everybody.

15:27.597 --> 15:29.767
[WOMAN] Why did you summon
all of us here?

15:29.857 --> 15:31.357
[TÖREGENE]
There are only young girls.

15:31.437 --> 15:33.357
Are you Dayir Usun?

15:33.817 --> 15:35.687
We serve under Prince Ögedei,

15:35.777 --> 15:37.527
the third son of the Khan.

15:38.157 --> 15:39.907
Our role is at the rear
of the army,

15:39.987 --> 15:41.777
keeping watch over the supplies.

15:41.867 --> 15:44.827
Ah, sounds like
I can rest assured then.

15:44.907 --> 15:46.827
These girls are
in your hands now.

15:46.907 --> 15:48.577
-[all gasp]
-Chieftain Dayir!

15:49.627 --> 15:51.837
After a long discussion,
we have decided

15:51.917 --> 15:54.007
to hand all of you over
to the Mongol nobles.

15:54.087 --> 15:55.377
No! Why?

15:55.467 --> 15:58.717
Come now, my dear.
You must listen carefully.

15:59.007 --> 16:01.047
The Mongols may have
spared us our lives,

16:01.137 --> 16:03.137
but that's where
their courtesy ends.

16:03.217 --> 16:06.177
They haven't yet forgiven us
for past confrontations.

16:06.267 --> 16:07.557
-[breathes shakily]
-I've no doubt

16:07.637 --> 16:09.187
we'll soon be reduced to slaves.

16:09.727 --> 16:11.647
But you aren't
like the rest of us.

16:12.357 --> 16:14.357
You have your whole lives
ahead of you,

16:14.437 --> 16:17.567
so go on
and find true happiness.

16:19.197 --> 16:20.527
As for you lot...

16:20.617 --> 16:21.697
Just make sure

16:21.777 --> 16:23.617
you tell your prince
and your Khan

16:23.697 --> 16:25.407
that these women
are no longer Merkits

16:25.497 --> 16:27.407
from this moment forward, yes?

16:27.497 --> 16:28.997
Do you understand me?

16:29.077 --> 16:31.287
[stutters] I'll pass it on.

16:31.627 --> 16:32.587
[SOLDIER] Huh?

16:33.707 --> 16:35.167
-[DAYIR] Töregene.
-Huh?

16:35.627 --> 16:37.087
Open your hand.

16:42.387 --> 16:43.927
This is a Jada stone.

16:44.387 --> 16:46.887
You can bring forth
storms with it.

16:46.967 --> 16:49.267
Wish that I had
a better parting gift.

16:49.347 --> 16:51.137
It's all I have left.

16:52.437 --> 16:55.607
You've brought me nothing
but joy. I'm grateful.

16:55.687 --> 16:56.937
[Töregene gasps softly]

16:57.527 --> 16:58.527
[DAYIR] Farewell.

17:00.107 --> 17:02.027
Live on with a smile.

17:10.907 --> 17:12.417
[TÖREGENE] It was eerily quiet

17:12.497 --> 17:14.377
in the middle
of that fateful night.

17:17.087 --> 17:18.417
[SOLDIER 1] Ready the horses!

17:18.507 --> 17:20.257
-Hurry!
-[SOLDIER 2] Right away!

17:21.167 --> 17:23.427
-[panting]
-[panicked chatter]

17:25.637 --> 17:27.307
[TÖREGENE]
The sky was burning...

17:27.387 --> 17:29.137
Soaked in blood.

17:29.217 --> 17:32.267
An unearthly sight the likes
of which I'd never seen.

17:32.727 --> 17:34.227
[SOLDIER 1]
What's happening out there?

17:34.307 --> 17:35.647
[SOLDIER 2] A rebellion.

17:35.727 --> 17:37.317
The captives have dug in
on the mountain.

17:37.937 --> 17:40.187
Prince Ögedei's army
is about to move out.

17:40.277 --> 17:42.697
-That vile Dayir Usun.
-[whimpers]

17:42.777 --> 17:45.567
You can never take Merkits
at their word.

17:45.657 --> 17:46.907
-[TÖREGENE] Move it.
-[grunts]

17:47.657 --> 17:48.907
-Chuu!
-[horse neighs]

17:48.987 --> 17:50.577
[SOLDIER] Hey! Wait!

17:54.497 --> 17:55.997
[TÖREGENE]
Even though the Mongols

17:56.087 --> 17:57.417
had shown them
all forgiveness...

18:00.257 --> 18:01.627
deep inside,

18:01.717 --> 18:04.007
they had never once forgiven
their oppressors.

18:04.547 --> 18:07.387
[DAYIR] We were raised
as hunters of the forest,

18:07.467 --> 18:09.927
and we won't ever be
a sheep herder's slave.

18:10.637 --> 18:13.017
Go on and find true happiness.

18:13.767 --> 18:15.807
[TÖREGENE]
Were those words a lie as well?

18:16.267 --> 18:19.277
No. I feel certain
that he truly meant them.

18:20.027 --> 18:20.977
Which is why

18:21.477 --> 18:23.647
he hadn't told me about
what he was planning to do.

18:26.907 --> 18:29.737
Except... I'm afraid
Chieftain Dayir

18:29.827 --> 18:31.237
made a grave oversight.

18:32.077 --> 18:33.367
After everything else,

18:33.457 --> 18:36.417
he failed to see
just how much...

18:37.207 --> 18:38.247
I loved him.

18:38.337 --> 18:40.047
[Töregene panting]

18:48.677 --> 18:49.967
[gasps]

18:50.847 --> 18:52.637
[ÖGEDEI] Oh, that's right.

18:53.807 --> 18:57.857
The soul of a kam
can rise up to the heavens.

18:57.937 --> 19:01.977
And by puncturing his body,
I only helped it escape.

19:03.317 --> 19:05.527
A red river in the sky.

19:05.607 --> 19:06.527
Uh?

19:07.027 --> 19:08.157
♪

19:10.867 --> 19:12.237
[ÖGEDEI] Who are you?

19:12.987 --> 19:13.997
Uh?

19:14.077 --> 19:15.077
[chuckles]

19:17.207 --> 19:19.917
[ILÜGE] Hold on.
What are you doing here?

19:19.997 --> 19:23.087
[TÖREGENE] Their rebellion
was put down all too easily.

19:24.337 --> 19:27.047
I later discovered
that they'd killed Qultuqan,

19:27.127 --> 19:28.717
and the others as well.

19:31.007 --> 19:33.217
Upon Genghis Khan's
return from battle,

19:33.967 --> 19:36.637
Khulan learned
of the uprising they attempted.

19:37.887 --> 19:39.977
And the moment
she heard the news...

19:40.057 --> 19:40.937
Uh?

19:43.107 --> 19:46.527
My father brought his fate
upon himself with such folly.

19:46.607 --> 19:50.737
The majesty of the Khan
is something nobody can tarnish.

19:50.827 --> 19:51.827
[Töregene gasps]

19:52.367 --> 19:53.537
[TÖREGENE] Khulan...

19:53.827 --> 19:56.747
How could you say those
awful things wearing a smile?

19:57.207 --> 19:58.367
After that,

19:58.747 --> 20:02.087
I was made Ögedei's wife
and allowed to live.

20:04.747 --> 20:06.207
[infant crying]

20:07.547 --> 20:09.717
[TÖREGENE] I gave birth
to his children as well.

20:10.637 --> 20:12.807
And the days passed by
rather peacefully.

20:14.307 --> 20:16.517
Yet all this time,
I've been waiting...

20:17.267 --> 20:20.397
Secretly hoping
for a raging storm to descend,

20:20.477 --> 20:22.607
and ravage this empire.

20:23.227 --> 20:24.817
I saved you earlier

20:24.897 --> 20:26.857
because your smile
seemed familiar.

20:27.487 --> 20:30.317
From that first day,
I saw Khulan in you.

20:30.697 --> 20:32.577
After all these years,

20:32.657 --> 20:35.827
I know how sad and powerless
she must have felt inside.

20:36.827 --> 20:37.827
But still...

20:38.457 --> 20:40.877
she understood what she needed
to do and fulfilled her role.

20:41.417 --> 20:43.587
Back then, I should've known

20:43.667 --> 20:45.707
how she was actually feeling,
and yet...

20:45.797 --> 20:47.087
[Sitara breathes uneasily]

20:48.127 --> 20:49.217
-So tell me...
-[gasps]

20:49.667 --> 20:51.177
...who are you really?

20:51.587 --> 20:53.597
[stutters] I'm, uh...

20:54.597 --> 20:55.887
That's all right.

20:55.967 --> 20:58.057
Regardless of who you may be,
you still can't--

20:58.137 --> 20:59.637
I spoke
to Princess Sorghaghtani.

21:00.767 --> 21:02.557
According to what she said,

21:02.647 --> 21:06.567
there is an imbalance of power
between Tolui and the Kha'an.

21:06.647 --> 21:08.027
In other words,

21:08.107 --> 21:10.567
the empire has never been
weaker than it is right now.

21:10.647 --> 21:12.447
Then you must be...

21:14.237 --> 21:17.237
My name is Sitara. I am a slave.

21:17.827 --> 21:19.327
The Mongol army
attacked our city

21:19.407 --> 21:20.747
and killed my mistress,

21:20.827 --> 21:23.167
then stole a book
that was precious to her.

21:23.247 --> 21:25.957
To honor her memory,
my final duty should have been

21:26.047 --> 21:27.957
getting her book back,
and yet...

21:28.047 --> 21:31.667
The thought that resistance
could cause further tragedy...

21:32.547 --> 21:34.007
That is my fear.

21:34.087 --> 21:37.007
And it's caused me
to lead a life without purpose.

21:37.097 --> 21:40.307
But this must be the moment
I've been waiting for.

21:40.387 --> 21:42.187
[gasps] How so?

21:42.267 --> 21:44.727
What could we hope
to accomplish?

21:44.807 --> 21:46.017
♪

21:51.027 --> 21:52.947
I have great knowledge.

21:53.697 --> 21:54.737
If you'll allow,

21:55.117 --> 21:57.197
I'll serve you as your
new Jada stone, Highness.

21:58.447 --> 22:01.327
Please, just lend me your power.

22:03.287 --> 22:06.707
And the two of us can summon
a fierce storm.

22:09.207 --> 22:11.047
[♪ closing theme song playing]

23:39.297 --> 23:41.557
[SITARA (ADULT)]
Next time, "Brothers."
